worlds in src/worlds/index.js: 471  ·  descriptions: 472
  reindeer-cyclone   'The Turning Herd' (wilderness)
      Each of some three thousand reindeer keeps to its own ring on a frozen lake. The outer ones trot, the inner ones walk, and at the centre calves lie in the snow round a boulder split in two by frost.
  manta-cyclone      'Inside the Manta Cyclone' (ocean)
      About two hundred manta rays turn in a single hollow column, and we rise up the inside of it against the turn, so that each animal arrives mouth first.
  stork-kettle-riso  'A Kettle of Storks' (sky)
      Migration day over a headland, storks circling up a thermal while ships cross below. All of it is printed in three inks, and the white of the birds is bare paper.
